                <pb facs="0549" n="477" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg477"/>

                <head>No. 289.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hamlin to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-07-10"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 10, 1882</date>.
                        (Received July 27, 1882.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 62.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your instruction No. 49, and
                    to my dispatch No. 38, relating to the duty imposed on live fish imported into
                    the Island of Cuba in foreign bottoms, I have now the honor to inclose herewith,
                    for your further information, a copy and translation of a note, dated the 3d
                    instant, upon the subject from the minister of state, by which it will be
                    observed that the subject has been referred to the governor-general for report,
                    which, when received, will be transmitted to the legation.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HANNIBAL HAMLIN.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d353-a1.xml" xpointer="d353-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
